actions of ATP on Ca<sup>2+</sup>-dependent exocytosis in pancreatic beta cells. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>96</volume>:<fpage>760</fpage>&#x02013;765.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9892707</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal">Takahashi, N., T. Kishimoto, T. Nemoto, T. Kadowaki, and H. Kasai. <year>2002</year>. Fusion pore dynamics and insulin granule exocytosis in the pancreatic islet. <source>Science.</source> <volume>297</volume>:<fpage>1349</fpage>&#x02013;1352.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12193788</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal">Wei, S., T. Xu, U. Ashery, A. Kollewe, U. Matti, W. Antonin, J. Rettig, and E. Neher. <year>2000</year>. Exocytotic mechanism studied by truncated and zero layer mutants of the C-terminus of SNAP-25. <source>EMBO J.</source> <volume>19</volume>:<fpage>1279</fpage>&#x02013;1289.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10716928</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib33"><citation citation-type="journal">Zenisek, D., J.A. Steyer, M.E. Feldman, and W. Almers. <year>2002</year>. A membrane marker leaves synaptic vesicles in milliseconds after exocytosis in retinal bipolar cells. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>35</volume>:<fpage>1085</fpage>&#x02013;1097.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12354398</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>